Owner-confirmed: `D:\crusorAIagent` does not exist on the host at all (not merely "the repo is
elsewhere"), and `D:\pulseAIagent` does. The previous commit moved the 69 repo-root references and
deliberately left parent-only paths alone, because their validity was not established then. It is now,
so they move too — none of them can work as written.

* `D:\crusorAIagent\crusor-res\cancel-session-artifacts\CDP_test\...` — CDP_TEST_GUIDE.md (4 sites),
  the setup DESKTOP_AGENT_UI_CDP_VALIDATION.md cites by name
* `D:\crusorAIagent\browser-verify.png` — run-all.bat:55 and crusor-webview/e2e-verify.spec.ts:17
  (the spec's screenshot destination; still an absolute path outside the repo, a separate fragility
  left alone on purpose)
* the `--user-data-dir` argument and `file:///D:/crusorAIagent/playground` in
  docs/DESKTOP_MANAGER_REGISTRATION_VERIFY.md
* `D:\crusorAIagent\python_test.exe` — src/tests/TEST_AGENT_GUIDE.md
* `D:/crusorAIagent/...` — AGENT_HANDOFF.md
* `webapp/src/App.tsx` — two user-visible mock strings ("The workspace root: D:\..."), so the demo
  never displays a path that cannot exist
* docs/RENOVATION_2026-08-29.md — a dated log citing the old screenshot path. It was accurate when
  written and is dead now; a reader copying it would fail, so it moves with the rest.

`patches/*.patch` still carry the old strings, and must: they are byte-faithful exports of commits
already reviewed, and editing them would break `git am`. The docs-host-root patch message describes
these parent paths as left alone — true of that commit; this commit is the follow-up it asked for.

Verified: the combined sweep (lang-extractors + preview + bridge + desktop + search + harness) is
22 failed / 239 passed here AND at the pristine previous tip in a clean worktree — byte-identical, so
this pass changes no behaviour. All 22 are pre-existing in this sandbox (langgraph, typing_extensions,
the stale tracked `out/`).

